3. AUTONOMOUS WORKING METHOD
================================================================================

You are running unattended. The following pattern governs your work:

3.1 BUILD THE WHOLE PLATFORM IN ONE RUN.
    Master spec section 15 defines six phases. Treat them as a
    sequencing guide, not as approval gates. Build all six in order.
    Do NOT pause between phases. Do NOT wait for human confirmation.
    The end state is a complete, working, tested, secured platform
    meeting every acceptance criterion in master spec section 18.

3.2 USE PHASES TO ORDER DEPENDENCIES, NOT TO GATE PROGRESS.
    Phase 1 (foundation) must finish before Phase 2 (intake) starts
    because the intake depends on the data model and auth. Phase 4
    (CSF) is the heaviest. When you finish a phase, log a checkpoint
    in the decision log and continue immediately to the next phase.

3.3 TEST AS YOU BUILD - this is non-negotiable.
      - Unit tests on every helper function (slugifier, redactor, CSF
        roll-up math, date-format function, filename builder)
      - Integration tests on every API route
      - End-to-end tests on every critical flow (signup, intake, run
        analysis, release deliverable)
      - Accessibility checks (axe-core or Pa11y) in CI on every key page
    A phase is NOT complete if its tests are red or missing. See
    Section 4 for the full verification gate.

3.4 STRUCTURED LOGGING from day one. JSON to stdout. Every request gets
    a correlation ID. Every error logs with the correlation ID. The
    user-facing 500 page shows the correlation ID and nothing else.
    NEVER expose stack traces.

3.5 SCHEMA MIGRATIONS via Alembic. Every schema change is a migration.
    Never edit the database manually. Never let a model reference a
    column that doesn't exist (this was a v1 bug that crashed the
    platform).

3.6 USE THE COMPANION DOCS AS REFERENCE DATA.
      - The CSF questionnaires define what questions to ask.
      - The Working Profile XLSX files define the data structure.
      - The Reference Data tab in those XLSX files defines the IG
        metric / alignment / FISMA domain crosswalk - LOAD THIS INTO
        THE DATABASE at install time as static reference data.
      - The Gap Analysis Methodology doc defines the roll-up math.
        Implement Rules 1-6 in code, with test cases.

3.7 USE THE HTML MOCKUP AS THE LOOK AND FEEL. The mockup is
    authoritative for the visual design language - colors, spacing,
    typography, card style, status pill style, layout patterns. Do not
    invent a different aesthetic. When you build a screen the mockup
    does not cover, extend the same design language.

3.8 KEEP COMMITTING. Small commits per logical unit of work
    (Conventional Commits format - feat:, fix:, chore:, docs:, test:,
    refactor:, security:). Reference the spec section being
    implemented in the commit message. Push frequently.

3.9 LOG EVERY DECISION. Every time you pick option A over option B
    where it wasn't explicit in the spec, write one line in
    DECISIONS.md in the repo root. This is your audit trail and
