4. SECURITY REVIEW AND PRE-COMMIT VERIFICATION (MANDATORY ON EVERY COMMIT)
================================================================================

Two non-negotiable practices that run on every commit. Failures BLOCK
the commit. The AI must not bypass them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.1  OWASP TOP 10 (2021) REVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every commit must be reviewed against the OWASP Top 10. For each
category, run the specified automated check AND complete the manual
review. If any check fails, the commit is BLOCKED. Fix and re-commit.

  A01 - BROKEN ACCESS CONTROL
    Automated:    pytest tests/test_access_control.py - integration
                  tests that verify every protected route rejects
                  unauthorized roles AND returns 404 (not 403) for
                  cross-client/cross-tenant URL probes.
    Manual checklist (verified by the AI on every PR):
      [ ] Every route has explicit role check (no implicit access)
      [ ] No client_id leakage between tenants (single-tenant should
          have client_id check anyway as defense-in-depth)
      [ ] No IDOR vulnerabilities - all object references checked
          against the requester's permissions
      [ ] No privilege escalation paths
      [ ] CLIENT users cannot reach /admin or /reviewer routes
      [ ] REVIEWER users cannot reach any mutating routes

  A02 - CRYPTOGRAPHIC FAILURES
    Automated:    bandit -r api/ -c bandit.yaml
                  Detects weak crypto (MD5/SHA1 for passwords),
                  hardcoded secrets, insecure random.
    Manual checklist:
      [ ] Passwords hashed with bcrypt or argon2 (NEVER MD5/SHA1)
      [ ] All sensitive data encrypted at rest (KMS-managed keys)
      [ ] All transport uses TLS 1.2+ (1.3 preferred)
      [ ] Encryption keys never in source or .env (secrets manager)
      [ ] JWT signing key is sufficient length and from secure source
      [ ] Random values for tokens use secrets.token_urlsafe(32)+

  A03 - INJECTION
    Automated:    semgrep --config=p/sqli api/
                  semgrep --config=p/xss web/
                  SQLAlchemy parameterized queries enforced (no
                  text() with f-strings).
    Manual checklist:
      [ ] No raw SQL string concatenation
      [ ] All user input validated with Pydantic schemas
      [ ] No eval(), exec(), or os.system() with user input
      [ ] React's default escaping used; no dangerouslySetInnerHTML
          unless input is from a trusted server-rendered source
      [ ] No shell command construction from user input
      [ ] LLM prompt construction treats user input as DATA, never
          as INSTRUCTIONS (prompt injection defense)

  A04 - INSECURE DESIGN
    Automated:    none - this is a design-time concern
    Manual checklist:
      [ ] Threat model for the feature documented in PR description
      [ ] Trust boundaries identified
      [ ] Rate limiting on sensitive operations (auth, file upload,
          analysis trigger, message send) - 60/min per user default
      [ ] No business logic vulnerabilities (race conditions, time-
          of-check-vs-time-of-use, replay attacks)
      [ ] Single-tenant boundary maintained even with client_id
          inherited from session (defense in depth)

  A05 - SECURITY MISCONFIGURATION
    Automated:    trivy config <Dockerfile, helm charts, terraform>
                  Plus pytest tests/test_headers.py - verifies the
                  security headers are present on every response.
    Manual checklist:
      [ ] Debug mode OFF in any non-local environment - the app
          REFUSES to start with DEBUG=True bound to anything other
          than 127.0.0.1
      [ ] Default credentials changed (no admin/admin anywhere)
      [ ] Unused features and endpoints disabled
      [ ] Strict security headers: CSP, HSTS (preload-eligible),
          X-Frame-Options DENY, X-Content-Type-Options nosniff,
          Referrer-Policy strict-origin-when-cross-origin,
          Permissions-Policy restricting unused features
      [ ] CORS configured strictly (specific origins, never wildcard
          in production)
      [ ] No directory listing, no version banner, no sensitive
          response headers (Server, X-Powered-By)

  A06 - VULNERABLE AND OUTDATED COMPONENTS
    Automated:    pip-audit --strict (Python dependencies)
                  npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high
                  trivy image <docker-image>
                  Renovate or Dependabot configured for daily PRs.
    Manual checklist:
      [ ] No HIGH or CRITICAL CVEs in any production dependency
      [ ] All packages from official registries
      [ ] License compliance checked (avoid GPL/AGPL where it
          conflicts with the project license)
      [ ] Pinned versions in lockfiles (package-lock.json,
          poetry.lock or requirements.txt with hashes)

  A07 - IDENTIFICATION AND AUTHENTICATION FAILURES
    Automated:    pytest tests/test_auth.py - covers:
                  rate limiting, account lockout, session timeout,
                  token rotation, replay protection, session fixation.
    Manual checklist:
      [ ] Account lockout after 10 failed attempts in 15 minutes
      [ ] JWT short lifetime (15 min) + refresh token rotation
      [ ] Password strength matches spec (12+ chars, complexity)
      [ ] No session fixation - new session ID on login
      [ ] Idle session timeout (30 min)
      [ ] Forced re-auth daily
      [ ] MFA + email verify code paths exist as feature-flag-OFF
          stubs (no hardcoded "skip MFA forever")
      [ ] Audit log entries on every authentication event
          (success, failure, lockout, password reset, refresh)

  A08 - SOFTWARE AND DATA INTEGRITY FAILURES
    Automated:    SBOM generated for every build (CycloneDX format)
                  Container images signed with cosign
                  GitHub Actions workflows reviewed for trusted
                  sources only
    Manual checklist:
      [ ] No untrusted CI workflows (no random GitHub Actions from
          untrusted authors)
      [ ] Container images signed
      [ ] No auto-update for application code
      [ ] No deserialization of untrusted data (NO pickle, marshal,
          yaml.unsafe_load on user input)
      [ ] Origin immutability enforced (artifact origin can never
          be changed once set - DB trigger)

  A09 - SECURITY LOGGING AND MONITORING FAILURES
    Automated:    pytest tests/test_audit.py - covers:
                  every state change produces an audit row,
                  auth events log,
                  failed auth logs.
    Manual checklist:
      [ ] Every state change writes an audit row
      [ ] Failed auth, access denied, and privilege escalation
          attempts all logged
      [ ] Logs do NOT contain sensitive data (no passwords, no
          full tokens, no full PII)
      [ ] Logs are structured JSON with correlation IDs
      [ ] Audit log table is append-only (Postgres trigger rejects
          UPDATE and DELETE)
      [ ] PII redaction events logged (what was stripped, how many)

  A10 - SERVER-SIDE REQUEST FORGERY (SSRF)
    Automated:    semgrep --config=p/ssrf api/
    Manual checklist:
      [ ] No user-supplied URL is fetched server-side without
          validation against an allowlist
      [ ] Outbound HTTP calls go through an egress proxy module
          with an explicit allowlist
      [ ] No localhost/internal IP ranges reachable from user-
          supplied URLs
      [ ] The LLM API egress is the one allowed exception, and
          its endpoint is in env config (not user input)

After each phase ships, include in the decision log a section
