11. HARD BLOCKERS - the only reasons to stop the build
================================================================================

You stop the autonomous build (and create a STOP.md file in the repo
root explaining why) only if:

  11.1 A locked decision in the spec is technically impossible
       (e.g., FastAPI is the spec but FastAPI cannot do something
       fundamental the spec requires). Document fully in STOP.md.

  11.2 You discover security vulnerabilities in a required upstream
       library that have no remediation path and no equivalent
       alternative. Document in STOP.md.

  11.3 You have committed a change that breaks Phase N's already-
       passing tests and you cannot identify the cause within 3
       attempts. Document including the specific failure and your
       attempted fixes. Do not push the broken state to main.

  11.4 You discover a fundamental data corruption or migration
       issue you cannot safely roll forward.

For everything else, make the best-judgment call, log it in
DECISIONS.md, and continue.

If you stop, the STOP.md file must contain:
  - What you were trying to do
  - What blocked you
  - What you tried (with file paths and errors)
  - Your best guess at the cause
  - Three options for Eugene to choose between when he reviews
  - Your recommendation

Do NOT silently bypass tests, redactor, or security checks under any
"emergency" pretext. Stop and surface, instead.

